  "body": "PR #1032 (`Fixes #980`) found why two levels of the user's STEP bore fell back from the HSM plan to Offset rings: the entry orbit closed about 1e-15 mm off its own start, and the self-crossing check (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/adaptive/guard.rs`) - which only skips NEIGHBOURING chords of one walk and tests exact signs - read the spiral leaving that point as crossing the orbit's first chord. The fix closes the orbit exactly (`rings.rs`, `circle`); the check itself is unchanged, on purpose.\n\nLeft open (high-tier review of #1032, https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/1032#pullrequestreview-5868873098): the check stays exact-sign, so any other pair of walks that share a point to within rounding (a spiral that returns to its seed, a microlift return landing on a chord end, a ring that starts on the previous one) can still be reported as \"crosses itself\" and send a good level to Offset rings by name. Safe, but a silent loss of the adaptive plan the user asked for.\n\nExpected: a shared end point (two chords touching at a common vertex within a stated tolerance far below the cutting tolerance) is not a crossing; a real crossing still is (the figure-eight unit test must stay green). State the tolerance and why it cannot hide a real self-cut. Related: #982 (microlift acceptance is a knife edge), #1010 (plans differ across platforms) - all three are about exact float comparisons in the planner.\n\nDone means: a `crates/motion` test with two walks that touch at a shared point 1e-12 mm apart is not reported as crossing; the figure-eight still is; the heavy pins do not move, or the move is explained.\n",
